[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am trying to understand Mathlib's convention on simpNF regarding <code>⁻¹</code>. Consider the following example #<strong><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Subgroup/Pointwise.html#Subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff\">Subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff</a></strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smul_mem_smul_set_iff</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mem_inv_smul_set_iff</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>These three lemmas can be very well replaced by a single simp lemma (the second one)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and the other two will follow from <code>by simp</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I was told that the RHS of a @[simp] lemma should be simpler than the LHS in most cases. Some consider <code>⁻¹</code> as more complicated. This is true for lemmas like <code>g • x = y ↔ x = g⁻¹ • y</code> since there is no priority on <code>x</code> or <code>y</code> and RHS indeed looks more complicated (so no @[simp]). However, I don't think this philosophy applies to the above case for the following reasons:<br>\n1) <code>⁻¹</code> is one of the most basic forms that you expect to things to cancel each other from simp lemmas and <code>⁻¹</code> is cheap.<br>\n2) the above example shows that allowing <code>⁻¹</code> on the RHS could reduce the number of lemmas. In principle, we can just keep the <strong>primitive</strong> lemma <code>x ∈ a • S ↔ a⁻¹ • x ∈ S</code> as a <code>simp</code> lemma and <code>x ∈ a⁻¹ • S ↔ a • x ∈ S</code> as a <code>rw</code> lemma, and abandon the first <code>a • x ∈ a • s ↔ x ∈ s</code>.<br>\n3) there is a good reason for pushing the <code>smul</code> from <code>A : set G</code> to the element <code>x : G</code>. We may reduce some work to the elementwise <code>smul</code> API and elementwise <code>smul</code> is usually easier to unfold when one wants to expose the concrete action formula.<br>\n4) <code>x ∈ a • S ↔ a⁻¹ • x ∈ S</code> is easier to trigger and use.<br>\nEdit: Thanks to Yaël for reminding me that my original example <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.smul_mem_smul_set_iff#doc\">docs#Set.smul_mem_smul_set_iff</a> is outdated</p>\n<p>Here is another example I want to discuss #<strong><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/FiniteIndex.html#Rep.indToCoindAux_mul_fst\">Rep.indToCoindAux_mul_fst</a></strong> where we construct a linear map between induced representation and coinduced representations from given data <code>{S : Subgroup G} (A : Rep.{w} k S)</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux_mul_fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This could be very well replaced by</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux_mul_fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indToCoindAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The RHS <code>indToCoindAux A g₁ (A.ρ s⁻¹ a) g₂</code> is extracting information from the <strong>primitive</strong> data <code>A : Rep.{w} k S</code>. Again, it's easier to trigger and use.</p>",
        "id": 624876916,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1789632394
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Getting rid of pointwise multiplication does seem like a simplification to me. I'm not knowledgeable enough to comment on your second example.</p>",
        "id": 624893050,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1789636518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1097608\">Jiaxi Mo</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.E2.81.BB.C2.B9.20simpNF.20convention/near/624876916\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>These three lemmas can be very well replaced by a single simp lemma (the second one)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That is incorrect, because <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem#doc\">docs#Set.mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem</a> requires <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Group#doc\">docs#Group</a> whereas <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.smul_mem_smul_set_iff#doc\">docs#Set.smul_mem_smul_set_iff</a> merely needs <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsLeftCancelSMul#doc\">docs#IsLeftCancelSMul</a></p>",
        "id": 624905318,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1789639290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> That's a good point. But the current Mathlib version assumes <code>variable [Group α]</code></p>",
